WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.839 --> 00:00:04.159
The risks of regression to war in post-conflict

00:00:04.239 --> 00:00:07.439
societies is high when the government

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:10.839
and the international community are not able

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.879
to make strong efforts at key moments

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:16.200
and sustain them over time.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.280
When we took office,

00:00:24.879 --> 00:00:28.720
there was no electricity and no water.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:32.039
Schools and clinics had crumbled,

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.519
roads were impassable, institutions of governance

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.600
had completely collapsed.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.280
In July of this year, we were able to turn on electricity

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.439
and water to parts of our capital city, Monrovia,

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:53.200
for the first time in fifteen years.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.759
But time is pressing.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.439
If our international partners wait too long

00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:10.239
to ramp up its support, then we may lose

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:14.879
the best chance Liberia has had in a generation

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.680
to end the conflict permanently

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:21.759
and build the foundations for growth and prosperity.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.800
We cannot afford to let that happen.

00:01:33.879 --> 00:01:36.639
Liberians are resilient people.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:39.479
They just want the simple things

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.879
that most people take for granted:

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.560
to live their lives in peace, get a good education,

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:50.920
to be able to provide for their families.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:57.439
These things are not too much for Liberians to dream about.

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:02.560
Poverty reduction strategies are at the core

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.560
of both averting a return to conflict and establishing

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:10.439
the foundation for sustained development.

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:15.039
We are placing emphasis on empowering the people,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.839
especially the poor and vulnerable,

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:22.319
to become participants in a development process.

00:02:22.639 --> 00:02:26.639
Education is central to renewal and reconciliation.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.119
No nation can develop under conditions

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.839
of a 70 percent illiteracy rate.

00:02:34.759 --> 00:02:37.639
Liberia is not a poor country,

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.079
but a country that has been poorly managed.

00:02:41.439 --> 00:02:43.879
We are committed to change this,

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.759
to pursue those goals that will move us

00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:52.159
from the crises of the past to the opportunity of the present.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.639
We are committed as a people to build a new Liberia

00:02:57.839 --> 00:03:01.360
from the ashes of an old, turbulent past

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.319
to a future of hope and promise.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.159
Thank you.

